				note="From docs/endpoint-status.md, verified 11 September 2026" link={{ label: 'Read the endpoint notes', href: `${repo}/blob/main/docs/endpoint-status.md` }} changes={[
					{ icon: 'globe', title: 'Hosts read from the official config at launch', was: 'hosts baked into constants' },
					{ icon: 'swap', title: 'Courses at api.polimi.it/iae/v1/insegn/', was: 'www22.dmz.polimi.it/iae/rest/v1/insegn' },
					{ icon: 'clock', title: 'Timetable at api.polimi.it/agenda', was: 'polimiapp…/polimi_app/agenda/api/me/{m}/events' },
					{ icon: 'lock', title: 'Sign-in scopes fetched from /jaf/oauth/params', was: 'a scope list frozen in 2023' },
					{ value: '9', title: 'scopes added upstream since then, picked up without a release', was: 'agenda among them, missing', tone: 'acid' },
					{ value: '2', title: 'scopes removed upstream', was: 'still requested', tone: 'orange' },
				]} />
		</Section>

		<Section split eyebrow="PoliVerse · Traps" title="Four things that looked like bugs." dim="None of them was ours."
			lead="Each one looked like a broken endpoint or a crash in the app. Each is written up, with what the app does about it.">
			<Findings columns={['Severity', 'What looked broken', 'When it shows', 'What PoliVerse does']} note="Severity 1 ends the student’s session or hides their data; severity 2 degrades one feature." items={[
				{ severity: 1, title: 'A missing scope looks like a dead endpoint.', text: 'A token minted without agenda signs in and works everywhere else, then gets 401 from the timetable.', impact: { label: 'After the paths were already fixed' }, fix: 'Build the sign-in request from the live scope list' },
				{ severity: 1, title: 'Two refreshes end the session.', text: 'The Politecnico rotates the refresh token, so a second refresh in flight presents one the first just invalidated.', impact: { label: 'Whenever two requests find the token expired together' }, fix: 'TokenStore is an actor: one refresh, everyone awaits it' },
				{ severity: 2, title: '“Code 6” is not a refusal.', text: 'The exams service answers “Utente non abilitato Code: 6”.', impact: { label: 'Between one exam session and the next' }, fix: 'Report the service as refused, keep the stale copy, never sign out' },
				{ severity: 2, title: 'Switching career fails upstream.', text: 'careerChange errors for this account, and not only in PoliVerse.', impact: { label: 'In the official app too, reproduced 12 September' }, fix: 'Set the favourite career, then sign in again' },
			]} />
		</Section>

		<Section id="cie" split eyebrow="PoliVerse · Signing in" title="CieID doesn’t know who called it." dim="So we tell it."
			lead="Inside a plain web view, CieID returns the authenticated session to Safari and the login is lost. PoliVerse intercepts the hand-off before the web view follows it, and re-opens it with a sourceApp that brings the student back.">
			<CodeSteps file="docs/cie-login.md · the flow" code={cieFlow} lang="txt" meta={[{ label: '4 steps', icon: 'lines' }, { label: 'CieIDBridge', icon: 'code' }, { label: 'Card + PIN', icon: 'lock' }]} steps={[
				{ title: 'Catch the link.', text: 'The login page navigates to the CIE identity provider; the web view sees it first.', lines: '1-2' },
				{ title: 'Re-open it with sourceApp.', text: 'The navigation is cancelled and opened in CieID with the app’s URL scheme attached.', lines: '3-4' },
				{ title: 'Come back to the app.', text: 'CieID returns to PoliVerse, and CieIDRouter carries the URL from onOpenURL to the live web view.', lines: '5-6' },
				{ title: 'Finish in the same web view.', text: 'The URL is stripped and loaded where the session lives, so the login simply continues.', lines: '7-9' },
			]} />
		</Section>

		<Section id="data" split eyebrow="PoliVerse · Freshness" title="A stale answer with a date" dim="says more than an empty screen."
			lead="The Politecnico’s servers send no ETag, no Last-Modified, no Cache-Control and no push, so freshness is the app’s job. Every Store publishes its cached copy on the first frame, a five-minute window decides whether to fetch, and the app revalidates when it returns to the foreground or comes back online.">
			<StateMachine label="A load through a Store" forbidden="clear the screen · never"
				before={[{ name: 'Cached', text: 'The offline copy is published at once.' }, { name: 'Refreshing', text: 'The load window says a fetch is due.' }]}
				fork={[{ name: 'Fresh', text: 'Decoded, cached, published, widgets told.', tone: 'blue' }, { name: 'Failed', text: 'Recorded beside the stale copy.', tone: 'orange' }]}
				after={[{ name: 'On screen', text: 'Silent under 15 minutes old, dated past that.', tone: 'dark' }]}
				labels={{ before: [['window due', 'cache first']], fork: ['200', 'error'], join: ['publish', 'keep the old copy'] }} />
		</Section>

		<Section tone="dark" split eyebrow="PoliVerse · Architecture" title="Four layers," dim="pulled apart."
			lead="Screens never talk to the network. Each service is a Source behind a Store, and one HTTP door leads out, to hosts the official config names.">
			<ExplodedStack layers={[
				{ name: 'Features', tint: 'acid', chips: [{ label: 'Today' }, { label: 'Courses' }, { label: 'Career' }], text: 'Seventeen feature folders, routed by ShellState, drawn with the look in use.' },
				{ name: 'Models', tint: 'violet', chips: [{ label: 'Career' }, { label: 'Agenda' }, { label: 'WeBeep' }], text: 'Feature models compose stores into the shapes screens consume.' },
				{ name: 'Stores', tint: 'blue', chips: [{ label: 'Source → Store → OfflineStore' }], text: 'Cache first, load window, offline copy in the app group, and a phase every screen can show.' },
				{ name: 'Services', tint: 'paper', chips: [{ label: 'PoliMi' }, { label: 'WeBeep' }, { label: 'Rooms', accent: true }], text: 'Servizi Online, Manifesti, WeBeep’s Moodle and the public rooms, through PoliMiAPI and PublicHTTP.' },
			]} />
		</Section>

		<Section>
			<Declaration project="PoliVerse · 2026" breadcrumb={['PoliVerse', 'The data layer', 'Store']} kind="Class" name="Store"
				abstract="Drives one Source: publishes its cached copy at once, refreshes when its load window says so, and never clears what is already on screen."
				availability={[{ label: 'iOS 27' }, { label: 'Swift 6 · MainActor' }, { label: 'Widgets · Watch' }, { label: 'DocC', muted: true }]}
				declaration="final class Store<S: Source>"
				nav={[{ title: 'The data layer', symbols: [{ name: 'Source', kind: 'P' }, { name: 'Store', kind: 'C', current: true }, { name: 'OfflineStore', kind: 'C' }, { name: 'LoadWindow', kind: 'S' }, { name: 'DataStatus', kind: 'C' }] }, { title: 'Sign-in', symbols: [{ name: 'Session', kind: 'C' }, { name: 'ServiceDirectory', kind: 'C' }, { name: 'CieIDBridge', kind: 'E' }, { name: 'CieIDRouter', kind: 'C' }] }]}
				mentioned={[{ label: 'CieID doesn’t know who called it', href: '#cie' }, { label: 'A stale answer with a date', href: '#data' }]}>
				<p>A <code>load()</code> reads the cache and publishes it, asks the <code>LoadWindow</code> whether a refresh is due, fetches and decodes through the one HTTP door, writes the copy back to the app group and tells the widgets. The outcome lands in <code>DataStatus</code>, so the app can always say <b>how old what it is showing is</b>. A failed load does not mark the window, so the next appearance tries again.</p>
			</Declaration>
		</Section>

		<Section id="decisions" tone="sand" eyebrow="PoliVerse · Decisions" title="Written down," dim="each with its reason." index={6}>
			<Principles rules={[
				{ title: 'Read, never write.', text: 'No enrolling, no refusing a mark, no forum posts, no hand-ins. The write requests are unverified, and a wrong one costs the student a session.', source: 'docs/writes-to-university-systems.md' },
				{ title: 'Never pass sample data off as real.', text: 'Sample data is on by default and every screen says so; all of it comes from one fictional degree, so career, timetable and courses agree.', source: 'SampleDegree · DataStatusLine' },
				{ title: 'Keep what is on screen.', text: 'A failed refresh leaves the cached copy in place and says how old it is.', source: 'Store · FreshnessBar' },
				{ title: 'Nothing leaves the phone on its own.', text: 'No analytics service and no crash reporter. Diagnostics and MetricKit reports stay on the device until the student shares them.', source: 'Diagnostics · docs/field-performance.md' },
				{ title: 'Borrow nothing that isn’t ours.', text: 'No SF Symbols in the icon, as Apple’s terms require, and nothing from the Politecnico’s identity: the app is unofficial and must not look otherwise.', source: 'design/app-icon/README.md' },
				{ title: 'Check every colour.', text: 'The brand navy is 13:1 on white but 1.3:1 on the dark background, so every accent has a dark twin. The worst pair is now 4.7:1.', source: 'Theme.swift' },
			]} example={{ label: 'Rule 03, drawn', dont: { title: 'Don’t clear the screen when a refresh fails', text: 'The student loses what was there, and learns nothing about why.' }, do: { title: 'Keep the copy, and date it', text: 'The cached timetable stays, with a line saying how old it is and that the refresh failed.' } }}>
				<Fragment slot="dont"><span class="st-state">Cached</span><span class="st-arrow-label">refresh fails →</span><span class="st-state uncertain">Empty screen</span></Fragment>
				<Fragment slot="do"><span class="st-state">Cached</span><span class="st-arrow-label">refresh fails →</span><span class="st-state dark">Cached · 40 min old</span></Fragment>
			</Principles>
		</Section>

