				{ q: 'Is it an official app?', a: 'No. PoliVerse is unofficial and not endorsed by Politecnico di Milano; the icon deliberately carries nothing from its identity.' },
				{ q: 'Where does the data come from, without a public API?', a: 'From the backend behind the official app. PoliVerse reads the same public config for its service hosts and its sign-in scopes, so a moved backend needs no release.' },
				{ q: 'Why can’t I enrol in an exam from it?', a: 'A wrong write costs a student a session; a wrong read costs a refresh. The request shapes are not verified, so writes stay out until they are.' },
				{ q: 'Why is the interface in Italian?', a: 'Because its students are. PoliVerse is written in Italian first and translated into English; the illustrations on this page show the Italian interface.' },
				{ q: 'Can I try it without a PoliMi account?', a: 'Yes. Sample data is on by default, and every screen says so while it is.' },
